.TH "OSTRYA\-PULL\-LOCAL" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-pull\-local \- Import refs and their objects from another local repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya pull\-local [OPTIONS] [SRC_REPO] [REFS]...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import refs and their objects from another local repository.
.PP
The command opens \%SRC_REPO and imports each ref, the commits that \%\-\-depth reaches, and the objects that these commits reach. When the link is possible, the pull hardlinks an object of the source into this repository. The pull writes local refs, or remote refs under \%\-\-remote. With \%\-\-remote, the verification keys of the remote apply to the pull. With \fB\%[ex\-ostrya] keep\-detached\-related=false\fR, it drops \fB\%ostrya.related\fR\&.
.PP
On success, the command prints one statistics line to standard output: \fB\%M metadata, C content objects imported; SIZE content written\fR\&. Under \%\-\-require\-static\-deltas, the line has the form of a pull from a remote. The command writes no progress line.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fISRC_REPO\fR
The repository to pull from. Required.
.TP
\fIREFS...\fR
The refs to pull.
.IP
With none, the pull takes every local ref of the source, under \fB\%refs/heads\fR\&.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fIREMOTE\fR
Write the pulled refs under this remote name.
.IP
The refs go to \fB\%refs/remotes/<remote>/<ref>\fR\&. Without this option, they are local refs. The verification keys of the \fB\%[remote "NAME"]\fR group apply to the pull, as they apply to \fB\%ostrya pull\fR (see \%ostrya\-config(1)). If the config has no group for the name, the pull makes only the checks that its switches ask for. Each switch wins over its key: \%\-\-gpg\-verify, \%\-\-gpg\-verify\-summary, \%\-\-sign\-verify, and \%\-\-sign\-verify\-summary turn a check on, and \%\-\-no\-gpg\-verify, \%\-\-no\-gpg\-verify\-summary, \%\-\-no\-sign\-verify, and \%\-\-no\-sign\-verify\-summary turn a configured check off. If the remote has the key \fB\%trust\fR, or if \%\-\-trust is given, the keys of the commits come from the trust group. The command then refuses \%\-\-gpg\-verify and \%\-\-sign\-verify, and \%\-\-no\-gpg\-verify and \%\-\-no\-sign\-verify turn off that check of the group.
.TP
\fB\-\-trust\fR \fINAME\fR
Take the keys of the commits from the trust group \fB\%[ex\-ostrya trust "NAME"]\fR (see \%ostrya\-config(1)).
.IP
The option wins over the key \fB\%trust\fR of the remote that \%\-\-remote names. It needs no \%\-\-remote, and \%\-\-remote still names the refs. With \%\-\-remote, the summary keys of the remote apply, and the command refuses a key of the remote that turns on a commit check. Without \%\-\-remote, the pull checks no summary, and the command refuses \%\-\-gpg\-verify\-summary. The command refuses \%\-\-gpg\-verify and \%\-\-sign\-verify, and \%\-\-no\-gpg\-verify and \%\-\-no\-sign\-verify turn off that check of the group.
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR \fIDEPTH\fR
The number of parents of each pulled commit to follow.
.IP
\%0 takes the commit alone, and \%\-1 takes the whole ancestry in the source. The command refuses a value less than \%\-1 before it reads a ref or an object of the source. Default: \%0.
.TP
\fB\-\-commit\-metadata\-only\fR
Import only the commit objects, and mark each commit partial.
.TP
\fB\-\-untrusted\fR
Verify the checksum of every imported object against its name.
.IP
Without this switch, the pull links or copies an object with no hash. An object that the pull writes again in another form always gets a hash. A mismatch fails the pull.
.TP
\fB\-\-bareuseronly\-files\fR
Reject regular files with mode bits outside \%0775.
.IP
The switch refuses a \%world\-writable, setuid, setgid, or sticky file. A symlink is exempt.
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-verify\-bindings\fR
Do not check the ref binding of a pulled commit.
.IP
Without this switch, the pull checks that the \fB\%ostree.ref\-binding\fR list of each pulled commit names the ref that it is pulled under. A commit with no binding key passes.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\-copy\fR
Copy every object, and make no hardlink.
.IP
Without this switch, the pull hardlinks an object of the source into this repository when the link is possible.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-localcache\-repo\fR \fILOCALCACHE_REPO\fR
Look in this repository for the objects that the source does not have.
.IP
The option can occur more than once. The pull reads the source first, and then each such repository in \%command\-line order. It takes an object from the first repository that holds it.
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-fsync\fR
Do not sync anything that this pull writes.
.IP
This switch changes no byte that the pull writes.
.TP
\fB\-\-per\-object\-fsync\fR
Sync the file of each content object when the pull stages it.
.IP
The pull does not sync metadata objects or hardlinked objects one by one. Without this switch, \fB\%[core] per\-object\-fsync\fR applies. \%\-\-disable\-fsync and \fB\%[core] fsync=false\fR win over this switch.
.TP
\fB\-\-gpg\-verify\fR
Require a GPG signature on every commit that the pull carries.
.IP
The pull uses the keys of the remote that \%\-\-remote names. Without \%\-\-remote, the command refuses this switch. The switch takes no value.
.TP
\fB\-\-gpg\-verify\-summary\fR
Require a GPG signature on the summary of the source.
.IP
The pull uses the keys of the remote that \%\-\-remote names. Without \%\-\-remote, the command refuses this switch. The switch takes no value.
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\-verify\fR
Require an \%ed25519 or spki signature on every commit that the pull carries.
.IP
The switch selects every engine of this build, and a valid signature of one engine is sufficient. The trusted keys come from the \fB\%verification\-<engine>\-key\fR and \fB\%verification\-<engine>\-file\fR keys of the remote that \%\-\-remote names, and from the system key store. The switch needs \%\-\-remote and takes no value.
.TP
\fB\-\-sign\-verify\-summary\fR
Require an \%ed25519 or spki signature on the summary of the source.
.IP
The switch selects every engine of this build, and takes the keys that \%\-\-sign\-verify takes. If the source has no \fB\%summary\fR or no \fB\%summary.sig\fR, the pull fails. The switch needs \%\-\-remote and takes no value.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-gpg\-verify\fR
Do not require a GPG signature on the commits.
.IP
The switch turns off the \fB\%gpg\-verify\fR key of the remote that \%\-\-remote names. With \%\-\-trust, or if the remote has the key \fB\%trust\fR, the switch turns off the GPG check of the trust group. It needs \%\-\-remote or \%\-\-trust, and conflicts with \%\-\-gpg\-verify.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-gpg\-verify\-summary\fR
Do not require a GPG signature on the summary of the source.
.IP
The switch turns off the \fB\%gpg\-verify\-summary\fR key of the remote that \%\-\-remote names. It needs \%\-\-remote and conflicts with \%\-\-gpg\-verify\-summary.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-sign\-verify\fR
Do not require an \%ed25519 or spki signature on the commits.
.IP
The switch turns off the \fB\%sign\-verify\fR key of the remote that \%\-\-remote names. With \%\-\-trust, or if the remote has the key \fB\%trust\fR, the switch turns off the \%sign\-api check of the trust group. It needs \%\-\-remote or \%\-\-trust, and conflicts with \%\-\-sign\-verify.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-sign\-verify\-summary\fR
Do not require an \%ed25519 or spki signature on the summary of the source.
.IP
The switch turns off the \fB\%sign\-verify\-summary\fR key of the remote that \%\-\-remote names. It needs \%\-\-remote and conflicts with \%\-\-sign\-verify\-summary.
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-static\-deltas\fR
Apply the static delta that the summary of the source advertises.
.IP
If the source advertises no delta for a commit, the command refuses the pull. The source must be an archive repository with a summary. The statistics line then has the form of a pull from a remote. This switch conflicts with \%\-\-disable\-static\-deltas.
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-static\-deltas\fR
Read no static delta.
.IP
Without \%\-\-require\-static\-deltas, the pull reads no static delta, so this switch changes nothing.
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
